          "text": "{\"regions\":{\"r2\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 34. \u092c\u0943\u0939\u0938\u094d\u092a\u0924\u093f\u2014from \u092c\u0943\u0939\u0924\u094d speech + \u092a\u0924\u093f the lord of; here the\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"planet Jupiter, \u0924\u0926\u094d\u092c\u0943\u0939\u0924\u094b\u0903 \u0915\u0930\u092a\u0924\u094d\u092f\u094b\u0936\u094d\u091a\u094b\u0930\u0926\u0947\u0935\u0924\u092f\u094b\u0903 \u0938\u0941\u091f\u094d \u0924\u0932\u094b\u092a\u0936\u094d\u091a V\u00e2rt. on\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"P\u00e2n. VI. I. 157. \u0938\u094d is substituted for the final of \u092c\u0943\u0939\u0924\u094d and \u0924\u0924\u094d\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"when followed by \u092a\u0924\u093f and \u0915\u0930 when the sense is a particular\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"deity and a thief respectively; so \u0924\u0924\u094d + \u0915\u0930 = \u0924\u0938\u094d\u0915\u0930. \u0938\u0902\u092d\u093e\u0935\u093f\u0924\u0903\u2014well\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"respected or esteemed i. e. of middle size.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"The Sanskrit grammatical quotation is somewhat unclear.\"},\"r3\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"\u0935\u093f\u0936\u0947\u0937\u0966\u2014see com; or \u0935\u093f\u0936\u093f\u0937\u094d\u092f\u0924 \u0907\u0924\u093f \u0935\u093f\u0936\u0947\u0937\u0903 unusual, uncommon; or\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"\u0936\u093f\u0937\u094d\u092f\u0924\u0947 \u0907\u0924\u093f \u0936\u0947\u0937\u0903\u0964 \u0935\u093f\u0917\u0924\u0903 \u0936\u0947\u0937\u0903 \u092f\u0938\u094d\u092f complete, hence uncommon; \u0935\u093f\u0936\u0947\u0937-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"\u0935\u093f\u0915\u094d\u0930\u092e\u0903 \u0935\u093f\u0936\u0947\u0937\u0966 \u0924\u0924\u094d\u0930 \u0930\u0941\u091a\u093f\u0903 \u092f\u0938\u094d\u092f bent on performing deeds of unusual\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"valour. \u0935\u0948\u0930\u093e\u092f\u0924\u0947 A denom. from \u0935\u0948\u0930 meaning \u0935\u0948\u0930\u0902 \u0915\u0930\u094b\u0924\u093f; derived\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"with the aff. \u0915\u094d\u092f\u0919\u094d; see com. \u092d\u093e\u0938\u094d\u0935\u0930\u094b brilliant. \u092d\u094d\u0930\u093e\u0928\u094d\u0924\u0903\u2014v. l. revol-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"ving; \u0915\u0930\u094d\u0924\u0930\u093f \u0915\u094d\u0924\u0903 by \u0917\u0924\u094d\u092f\u0930\u094d\u0925\u093e\u0915\u0930\u094d\u092e\u0915-&c. Pan. III. 4, 72. \u092a\u0930\u094d\u0935\u0928\u094d\u2014The\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":8,\"text\":\"time of new or full moon ( opposition or conjunction ). \u0936\u0940\u0930\u094d\u0937\u093e\u0935\u0966\u2014\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":9,\"text\":\"The allusion here is to the severance of the demon\u2019s head at the\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":10,\"text\":\"time when the nectar that was churned out of the ocean was\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":11,\"text\":\"served to the gods, and R\u00e2hu attempted to drink it by joining\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":12,\"text\":\"their line. The sun and the moon informed Vishnu of the\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":13,\"text\":\"fraud, whereupon he severed the demon\u2019s head with his\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":14,\"text\":\"discus. But as the demon had tasted a little quantity of\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":15,\"text\":\"amrita the head lived and is supposed to wreak its vengeance\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":16,\"text\":\"on the two luminaries. See Mat. Pu. Adh. II. 5. 13. 16. Bh\u00e2g.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":17,\"text\":\"P. VIII. 9. 23\u201326, The fig is \u0905\u092a\u094d\u0930\u0938\u094d\u0924\u0941\u0924\u092a\u094d\u0930\u0936\u0902\u0938\u093e as the action of\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":18,\"text\":\"R\u00e2hu which is not the matter in hand (\u0905\u092a\u094d\u0930\u0938\u094d\u0924\u0941\u0924) implies the\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":19,\"text\":\"action of an inveterate wicked man which is the matter intended\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":20,\"text\":\"to be described.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"Several Sanskrit words and the split compound at the beginning are not perfectly clear.\"},\"r4\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl, 35. \u092b\u0923\u093e\u092b\u0932\u0915 The flat surface of (extensive board for-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"med by ) his hoods. Comp. Mat. Pu. CCLIX. 7. \u092e\u0927\u094d\u092f\u0947\u092a\u0943\u0937\u094d\u0920\u092e\u094d\u2014on\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"the back. Avy. Comp. This is less common though by no\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"means very rare: comp. Bv. I. 60; Nai. III. 40; Sis III, 70\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"VII. 52 and 70 Bhatti V. 4. \u092a\u093e\u0930\u0947 \u092e\u0927\u094d\u092f\u0947 \u0937\u0937\u094d\u0920\u094d\u092f\u093e \u0935\u093e\u0964 P\u00e2n. II.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"1. 18. The words \u092a\u093e\u0930 and \u092e\u0927\u094d\u092f are optionally compounded\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"with a noun in the gen. case forming an Avy., the final \u0905 of\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":8,\"text\":\"\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":9,\"text\":\"these being irregularly (\u0928\u093f\u092a\u093e\u0924\u0928\u093e\u0924\u094d \u090f\u0926\u0928\u094d\u0924\u0924\u094d\u0935\u0902 \u091a\u093e\u0928\u092f\u094b\u0930\u094d\u0928\u093f\u092a\u093e\u0924\u094d\u092f\u0924\u0947\u0964 Sid.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":10,\"text\":\"Kau.) changed to \u090f; optionally there may be Gen. Tat. e. g.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"The citation on line 5 and parts of the Sanskrit quotation are damaged or indistinct.\"},\"r1\":{\"type\":\"page_number\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"( 17 )\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":false,\"note\":null},\"r5\":{\"type\":\"other\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"2\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":false,\"note\":null}},\"units\":[{\"id\":\"u1\",\"type\":\"notes\",\"number\":null,\"label\":null,\"open_start\":true,\"open_end\":true,\"children\":[\"u2\",\"u3\"]},{\"id\":\"u2\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"34\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r2\",\"r3\"]},{\"id\":\"u3\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"35\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":true,\"children\":[\"r4\"]}],\"flows\":[{\"flow\":\"main\",\"units\":[\"u1\"]}],\"relations\":[]}"
